  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "The value of $\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{1-\\cos (1-\\cos x)}{x^4}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "3ABte",
      "text": "\r\n$\\frac{1}{6}$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ObMgC",
      "text": "\r\n$\\frac{1}{8}$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "SawiN",
      "text": "\r\n$\\frac{1}{10}$\r\n",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Vxzvb",
      "text": "\r\n$\\frac{1}{12}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$1-\\cos (1-\\cos x)=2 \\sin ^2\\left(\\frac{1-\\cos x}{2}\\right)$\r\n$=2 \\sin ^2\\left(\\sin ^2 \\frac{x}{2}\\right)$\r\n$\\therefore \\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{1-\\cos (1-\\cos x)}{x^4}=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{2 \\sin ^2\\left(\\sin ^2 \\frac{x}{2}\\right)}{x^4}$\r\n$=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{2 \\sin ^2\\left(\\sin ^2 \\frac{x}{2}\\right)}{\\left(\\sin ^2 \\frac{x}{2}\\right)^2} \\times \\frac{\\sin ^4 \\frac{x}{2}}{\\left(\\frac{x}{2}\\right)^4 \\times 16}$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{8}$",
    "image": null
  },
